title the bench that was already occupied; REDS %281 fires a third time, caught at the door
prompt Keaton opened Sound on the macOS bench -- read Kyri and Gauge, honor the INNER LOOP, take the widened constellation lane core-first, hold the Pond accrete-only boundary, send the twice-pulled way, stop at the custody gates.
think I opened the lap the way the card asks -- Kyri, Gauge, ITINERARY whole, the top three index rows and the newest recommend line -- and then ran the cold roster before touching anything. The recommend line handed me a clear ungated kg: the 19-file socket-constant sweep, one module per lap with its own witness, plus the caravan_harvest comment whose text says a count is read without being asserted while the line below asserts a prefix of it.
think The survey came back clean and larger than the recommend named. Twenty .rye files declare SOL_SOCKET; one is the exemplar %282 already repaired. All nineteen of the rest carry BOTH legs of that red, not one: each spells const SOL_SOCKET: c_int = 1 with SO_REUSEADDR 2 and, where present, SO_RCVTIMEO 20, and each also hand-rolls sockaddr_in as an extern struct in the Linux layout rather than reaching c.sockaddr.in. So the sweep is the whole %282 repair applied nineteen times, and the right shape is subtraction rather than a new shared module: std.c already publishes these once and dispatches them on native_os, so the fix is to stop copying the table and ask the host. Every one of the nineteen has at least one tool naming it, so each can close on a witness.
think Then the concrete fact arrived and outranked the plan. git rev-list --count HEAD read 3529 against a HEAD of a2f485d53e, where the session opened at 85c76c84d -- same commit subject, different hash. The reflog names the cause without ambiguity: pull --rebase xy main, a rebase abort, a second pull --rebase, rebase continue, finish. Nothing in my session ran a single one of those.
think Measurement, not inference. A second claude process stands in this same checkout -- pid 2240, --model claude-fable-5 --effort xhigh, --resume=097f3e44-cf6b-44b7-9209-aa5b315eeb96, a different session id from my own 43387b2f. It started 02:20:52 and mine at 02:23:10, so the peer holds the bench by two minutes eighteen seconds and I am the one who arrived second. It is live right now: rishi run tools/ca/caravan_suite_witness.rish singing the 113-rung Caravan choir, tools/ca/caravan_address_space_witness.rish, tools/s/sow_witness.rish, and two rye build processes writing .zig shadows. Seventy-three .zig shadows stand in caravan/ as I read.
think That is REDS %281 exactly -- two agent sessions in one working tree racing on Rye's unlocked ephemeral .zig shadows -- and it is the third firing, after 20260826.211951 booked it and the same evening saw commit 7bd3cb949 sweep another session's staged ITINERARY diff. What is different this time is the direction: the first two were read backwards out of a false RED and a swept commit, and this one was read at the door, before a byte was written. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, and this is the third.
think The decisive reading is the card itself. construction/ITINERARY.md said Git nib 7ecb0b48d9 when I read it whole at lap open; twenty minutes later the same line reads 78233f407f; HEAD is a2f485d53e. Three numbers, one card, and no tree anywhere holds all three. The card I read is not the tree I stand on, which is the one precondition every other directive on that card assumes.
think So I stood down rather than worked around. I killed my own roster at pid 3395 -- it was contending for the same shadows the peer's choir needs, and its verdict was already void, since it recorded tree_at_open=51af03bbda36 while HEAD moved and rye/src/main.rye gained 87 uncommitted lines beneath it. I checked for the orphan the card warns about, where a killed rishi wrapper leaves its sh child behind: none, pgrep clean.
obs The three reds my killed roster printed before it stopped -- equinox_e123_living_pin_guard, exec_bit, nib_honesty -- are recorded here as unreadable rather than as findings. Their evidence files under construction/standing-equipment-reds/ read empty when I went to them, because they are being rewritten live. nib_honesty is very likely the peer's rebase showing through, since the card's nib and HEAD genuinely disagree. I am not booking any of the three. This is %281's blast radius said plainly: a choir's verdict becomes a coin toss, and an agent reading it books a fault that does not exist.
obs I wrote nothing to the tree beyond this log, and the reason is the expensive half of %281 rather than the cheap one. construction/REDS.md is modified in the working tree right now by the peer, one line changed. Booking a new REDS row from a second session in the same checkout would be REDS %230 and %252 performed on purpose -- two hands allocating one row number by reading one tree -- and the pin is at its byte wall besides. This firing belongs as evidence under the existing %281, which is where I have put it.
obs I did not run touch .loop-gates-only and did not print GATES-ONLY, and the distinction is worth being exact about. That signal says the agent-doable queue is empty and only the custody gates in ITINERARY remain. That is not true here: the queue holds the nineteen-file sweep, ungated and ready. What stands in front of it is an open red whose two answers are both Keaton's word -- a lock inside bridge_to_zig or a per-process shadow name, or one working tree per star. Printing GATES-ONLY would have told him his work was finished when the truth is that his bench is occupied.
obs The Pond accrete-only boundary was not approached; no ai-jail markdown was read or touched. The adaptation grant went unspent -- no bash, HTML, or Python stood in the way of anything. publish-seed.sh was not run and the seed cadence stays Dream's. Nothing was staged, committed, or pushed, so the twice-pulled send did not open.
obs Council rota N=3529 mod 5 = 4 -- Earth, Mercury, the concrete; last lap read row 0, so this is an honest advance rather than a repeat, and no hand-advance was needed. The row read as instruction. Earth's sense is aroma, the sense that arrives before argument, and the row exists to keep small hard checkable things small, hard, and checkable. This lap had exactly one such thing in it: three commit hashes that cannot name one tree, read off the card and the reflog at the door, before any reasoning about what to build. The row also names what to do when something smells wrong -- a stamp that outruns the clock, a page whose status names no room -- and a nib that names a commit the tree left behind is the same smell one column over.
